testinvalid.md:1:32:Prose.ZeroRelative:An object-relative clause without 'that' or 'which' compresses a relationship into a noun phrase. Rewrite it as a prepositional phrase or its own sentence; add the pronoun only when the clause does nothing but identify the noun.
testinvalid.md:3:23:Prose.ZeroRelative:An object-relative clause without 'that' or 'which' compresses a relationship into a noun phrase. Rewrite it as a prepositional phrase or its own sentence; add the pronoun only when the clause does nothing but identify the noun.
testinvalid.md:5:11:Prose.WarningVerbs:'holds' is a general verb; the relationship has its own word: contains, keeps, includes, lists, specifies, decides, is.
testinvalid.md:7:21:Prose.AbstractAbsence:'nothing to reformat' describes an exception as an abstract absence; say what happens instead.
testinvalid.md:9:26:Prose.ArrowChain:'host -> features' compresses a relationship into an arrow; write it as a sentence.
testinvalid.md:11:25:Prose.InventedAlternative:'rather than' contrasts with an alternative; keep it only where the alternative is real.
testinvalid.md:13:38:Prose.TrailingBenefit:The trailing ', ensuring' clause claims a benefit without the mechanism that produces it.
testinvalid.md:15:1:Prose.WarningVerbGerunds:'Naming' is a general verb; the relationship has its own word: contains, keeps, includes, lists, specifies, decides, is.
testinvalid.md:15:19:Prose.InventedAlternative:'rather than' contrasts with an alternative; keep it only where the alternative is real.
testinvalid.md:16:1:Prose.WarningVerbPhrases:'is used by both' is more specific than 'serve both'.
testinvalid.md:18:31:Prose.ZeroRelativePossessive:A noun followed by a possessive subject and a verb may be an object-relative clause without 'that' or 'which'. Such a clause compresses a relationship into a noun phrase: rewrite it as a prepositional phrase or its own sentence, and add the pronoun only when the clause does nothing but identify the noun.
testinvalid.md:20:1:Prose.ZeroRelative:An object-relative clause without 'that' or 'which' compresses a relationship into a noun phrase. Rewrite it as a prepositional phrase or its own sentence; add the pronoun only when the clause does nothing but identify the noun.
testinvalid.md:20:5:Prose.ZeroRelativeShort:A noun followed by a determiner, a noun and a verb may be an object-relative clause without 'that' or 'which'. Such a clause compresses a relationship into a noun phrase: rewrite it as a prepositional phrase or its own sentence, and add the pronoun only when the clause does nothing but identify the noun.
